    "legend": "PanNET of the pancreas tail (cm0,8; pT1, pN0, UICC 2017) associated with large haematoma due to previous endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) procedure in a patient with hypergastrinemia and duodenal ulcer (Zollilnger-Ellison syndrome, sporadic). The tumour displays the classical gyriform/trabecular structure with pseudorosettes in absence of necrosis and evident mitoses. Note the surrounding exocrine pancreas with active steatonecrosis and haematic suffusion.",
